\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A positive weight with a negative coefficient}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{On #{U(1)}, take #{0<\epsilon<1} and
##{k(e^{i\theta})=1-\epsilon\cos\theta
 =1-\frac\epsilon2 e^{i\theta}-\frac\epsilon2 e^{-i\theta}.}
This is a real continuous central function, unchanged by inversion,
and #{k\ge1-\epsilon>0}. Its character coefficients at
#{n=\pm1} are nevertheless #{-\epsilon /2}.
Thus the pointwise and Fourier positivity assumptions in the
[kernel definition](fdip-007I) are distinct.}
